id=a52sxq_wallpaper_boot_transition
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: lock screen wallpaper after boot (aborted boot transition left the wallpaper token hidden)
author=kusti420
description=Black lock screen from boot until the first unlock (9.3.53 log 2026-10-18; also the 9.3.48 and uvc7 boots). SurfaceFlinger shows the lock WallpaperWindowToken layer hidden from 09:46:08.764 to the unlock at 09:49:58.990 although the lock engine had drawn its frame and its window was visible. When both wallpapers are SpriteWallpaper live wallpapers, nothing binds SystemUI's ImageWallpaper early, so SystemUI starts after FallbackHome. Its ShellTaskOrganizer registration then waits the full 2 s TransitionController.runWhenIdle timeout behind the fallback FallbackHome OPEN transition (#2). Meanwhile KeyguardViewMediator's early setLockScreenShown is combined into the fallback CHANGE transition #3, which collects the wallpaper tokens: lock token visible requested true, then false, client visible true. WindowAnimator drops the surface update because the token is collecting. Shell registration then flushes (aborts) #3, and the abort path only resyncs containers whose requested visibility differs from the start of the transition (false == false here). Later the lock token is requested visible again, but WallpaperWindowToken.commitVisibility() returns early because the client is already visible, so the SurfaceControl stays hidden until the next transition that moves the wallpaper (keyguard going away). Fix: Transition.onTransactionReady's abort branch calls K4WallpaperAbort.onAborted(this). For each wallpaper token of the aborted transition that no other transition holds, it commits the not-requested ones to hidden (as finishTransition does for a played transition) and queues a surface visibility update, so WindowManager state and the SurfaceControl match again and the next adjustWallpaperWindows shows the lock wallpaper. logcat tag K4WallpaperAbort.
